---
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro"
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import { docsMetadata } from "@/lib/docs-meta"

const metadata = docsMetadata("/docs/ci/sharding")
---
<DocsLayout metadata={metadata}>
    <section>
      <h1 class="mt-0 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">Sharding and merging</h1>
      <p class="gz-prose gz-prose--lead mb-8">Every mutation runs your package&apos;s tests once, so a large module can keep one CI
        job busy for a long time. Split the run across parallel jobs, then merge the shards
        back into one report set that reads like a single run.</p>
      <div>
        <div id="run">
          <h2>1. Run each shard</h2>
          <p>Give every job the same <code>TOTAL</code> and its
            own <code>INDEX</code> with{" "}<code>-s INDEX/TOTAL</code>. Example with 3 jobs:</p>
          <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`gooze run -s 0/3 ./...
gooze run -s 1/3 ./...
gooze run -s 2/3 ./...`} />
          <p>Each job tests only its slice of the mutations and prints a score for that slice,
            not for the whole module.</p>
          <p class="">Shards are 0-based: the value must satisfy{" "}<code>0 &lt;= INDEX &lt; TOTAL</code>{" "}(<code>4/4</code> is an error). Each shard writes
            to <code>.gooze-reports/shard_INDEX/</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="merge">
          <h2>2. Collect and merge</h2>
          <p>Bring every <code>shard_*</code> directory back
            into one reports directory (in CI, upload each shard as an artifact and download them
            all in a final job), then merge. Results don&apos;t show up in the viewer until you do.
            After the merge, <code>gooze report view</code> shows one table and one score for
            the whole module, the same as an unsharded run would.</p>
          <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`gooze report merge
gooze report view`} />
          <p class="">Shard reports replace base reports for the same source file, and base reports for files
            no shard re-tested are kept, so the cache still works. Each shard&apos;s{" "}<code>gooze run</code> prints the score of its shard only; the merge prints the full
            score. Details:{" "}<a href="/docs/cli/report/#merge"><code>gooze report merge</code></a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="ci">
          <h2>Ready-made CI pipelines</h2>
          <p>Both provider guides wire these two steps into a pipeline:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/docs/ci/github/#sharded">GitHub Actions</a>:
              a <code>matrix</code> of shards plus a merge job.</li>
            <li><a href="/docs/ci/gitlab/#sharded">GitLab CI</a>:{" "}<code>parallel: N</code> plus a merge stage
              (note <code>CI_NODE_INDEX</code> is 1-based).</li>
            <li>To also skip unchanged files across runs, combine sharding with a shared baseline:{" "}<a href="/docs/ci/sharing-reports/">Sharing reports (OCI)</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
</DocsLayout>
